    "body": "Answers from the machine owner (2026-11-25):\n\n- **`G29` is not required.** It marks a restart point: if the wire does not thread at a start hole, the control skips forward to the next `G29`. That can help in a batch of parts with several start holes. Do not write it in the first version. A later option can add one `G29` before each start hole.\n- **`C001` is always the first cutting condition and always goes with `H001`.**\n- **After the first pass, the condition number is not fixed.** The condition for `H002` is not always `C002`: it comes from the operator's condition table at the control.\n\nWhat this changes:\n1. Pass 1 writes `C001` with `H001`.\n2. Pass 2 and later write `H00n` from the pass number. The `C` number for those passes must come from a per-pass value that the user sets. The default is `C00n`, and the setup sheet tells the operator to check it against the control's table. The post must not invent a condition number silently.\n\nBoth open questions in the issue body are now answered.\n",
